mn {\n    display: flex;\n    padding: 20px 60px 30px;\n    gap: 40px;\n  }\n\n  .methodology-col {\n    flex: 1;\n    border-right: 1px solid #ddd;\n    padding-right: 30px;\n  }\n\n  .results-col {\n    flex: 1;\n    padding-left: 10px;\n  }\n\n  .methodology-col h2,\n  .results-col h2 {\n    color: #e74c3c;\n    font-size: 22px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    margin-bottom: 15px;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n  }\n\n  .methodology-col ol {\n    padding-left: 20px;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n  }\n\n  .methodology-col ol > li {\n    margin-bottom: 8px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  .methodology-col ol > li > ol {\n    padding-left: 20px;\n    margin-top: 4px;\n  }\n\n  .methodology-col ol > li > ol > li {\n    font-weight: 400;\n    margin-bottom: 2px;\n  }\n\n  .results-col p {\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    color: #333;\n    margin-bottom: 12px;\n  }\n\n  .results-table {\n    width: 100%;\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    margin-top: 15px;\n    font-size: 13px;\n  }\n\n  .results-table thead th {\n    background: #e74c3c;\n    color: #fff;\n    padding: 10px 12px;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-weight: 600;\n    font-size: 13px;\n  }\n\n  .results-table thead th:first-child {\n    text-align: left;\n  }\n\n  .results-table tbody td {\n    padding: 7px 12px;\n    text-align: center;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #e8e8e8;\n  }\n\n  .results-table tbody td:first-child {\n    text-align: left;\n    font-style: italic;\n    background: #5bc0c8;\n    color: #fff;\n    font-weight: 500;\n  }\n\n  .results-table tbody tr:nth-child(even) td:not(:first-child) {\n    background: #f5f5f5;\n  }\n\n  .results-table tbody tr:nth-child(odd) td:not(:first-child) {\n    background: #fff;\n  }\n\n  .table-footer {\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    align-items: flex-end;\n    margin-top: 10px;\n    font-size: 12px;\n  }\n\n  .table-footer .r2 {\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 13px;\n  }\n\n  .table-footer .notes {\n    text-align: right;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n  }\n\n  .conclusion-section {\n    padding: 20px 60px 30px;\n  }\n\n  .conclusion-section h2 {\n    color: #e74c3c;\n    font-size: 22px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    margin-bottom: 12px;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n  }\n\n  .conclusion-section p {\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    color: #333;\n  }\n\n  .footer {\n    background: #1a1a1a;\n    color: #ccc;\n    padding: 25px 60px;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n  }\n\n  .footer strong {\n    color: #fff;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<div class=\"header\">\n  <h1>The sales effect of \"Free App of the Day\"<br>on Amazon Appstore: An empirical study</h1>\n  <div class=\"authors\">Hong Chen, Kevin Lachaud, Wenqi Zhou</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"intro-section\">\n  <div class=\"intro-text\">\n    <h2>Introduction</h2>\n    <p>Apps, as an abbreviation of mobile applications, are software products for mobile platforms (Tang, 2016). They are designed to perform certain tasks on mobile devices (Islam, Islam, &amp; Mazumder, 2010). This product category has grown to become a gigantic differentiated market with over 3.48 million apps on Google Play, an app marketplace, and the recent projection of over 935-billion-dollar revenue in 2023 (Statista Research, 2021a, Statista Research, 2021b).</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"intro-image\">\n    <div class=\"placeholder\">[Image: Hand holding smartphone with smartwatch]</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"objective-section\">\n  <h2>Objective</h2>\n  <p>This work studies the adverse effect of \"Free App of the Day\" at Amazon Appstore.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"two-column\">\n  <div class=\"methodology-col\">\n    <h2>Methodology</h2>\n    <ol>\n      <li>Literature review\n        <ol>\n          <li>Digital free sampling</li>\n          <li>eWOM</li>\n        </ol>\n      </li>\n      <li>Hypotheses\n        <ol>\n          <li>H1 - Online user decisions to adopt apps are discouraged by the price rebound after the zero-price offering of FAD ends. The sharper price rebound leads to a greater decrease in app adoptions.</li>\n          <li>H2 - Conditional on the total volume of eWOM, organic reviews are more influential to online user decisions of adopting apps than promotion-induced reviews after the FAD promotion ends.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </li>\n      <li>Data\n        <ol>\n          <li>Context and data collection</li>\n          <li>Key variables</li>\n        </ol>\n      </li>\n      <li>Empirical analysis\n        <ol>\n          <li>Exploratory analysis</li>\n          <li>Regression model and results</li>\n        </ol>\n      </li>\n    </ol>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"results-col\">\n    <h2>Results</h2>\n    <p>We notice that a few apps were off the direct spotlight post-promotion; however, they still offer zero price for another one or two days.</p>\n    <p>Specifically, an increase in SkewDaily<sub>i</sub> indicates a more right skewed distribution of daily number of reviews during the post-promotion period.</p>\n\n    <table class=\"results-table\">\n      <thead>\n        <tr>\n          <th>Empty Cell</th>\n          <th>Mean</th>\n          <th>S.D.</th>\n        </tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr>\n          <td>PriceRebound<sub>i,t</sub></td>\n          <td>−0.40***</td>\n          <td>0.06</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>SkewDaily<sub>i</sub></td>\n          <td>−0.19*</td>\n          <td>0.11</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>KurtDdaily<sub>i</sub></td>\n          <td>−0.09**</td>\n          <td>0.05</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>Ln(NumReviews<sub>i,t</sub>)</td>\n          <td>0.59***</td>\n          <td>0.08</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>AverageRating<sub>i,t</sub></td>\n          <td>2.06***</td>\n          <td>0.40</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>VarianceRating<sub>i,t</sub></td>\n          <td>1.17***</td>\n          <td>0.30</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>Day<sub>i,t</sub></td>\n          <td>−0.11*</td>\n          <td>0.03</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>Age<sub>i,t</sub></td>\n          <td>−0.0004***</td>\n          <td>0.0002</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>AppSize<sub>i,t</sub></td>\n          <td>0.01***</td>\n          <td>0.002</td>\n        </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n\n    <div class=\"table-footer\">\n      <div class=\"r2\">R2 = 0.45</div>\n      <div class=\"notes\">\n        * p &lt; 0.1.<br>\n        **p &lt; 0.05.<br>\n        ***p &lt; 0.01.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"conclusion-section\">\n  <h2>Conclusion</h2>\n  <p>We conclude that these promotion-induced reviews are less influential than organic reviews.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"footer\">\n  <strong>References:</strong> Chen, H., Lachaud, K. and Zhou, W., 2022. The sales effect of \"Free App of the Day\" on Amazon Appstore: An empirical study. Digital Business, 2(2), p.100020.\n</div>\n\n</body>\n</html>",
